# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list
# =============================================================================
# Every entry here MUST carry a justification and a removal condition. An
# unexplained ignore is indistinguishable from an unnoticed vulnerability.
# Re-check this file whenever `Security Scan` newly passes — an entry that no
# longer matches anything should be deleted, not left to rot.

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action
# Execution Before 400 Response" (HIGH). Installed 7.18.1; fixed in 8.3.0.
#
# Not exploitable in this application. The advisory is specific to React
# Server Components mode. This frontend is a client-only Vite SPA:
#   - src/main.tsx mounts <BrowserRouter>, not a data/RSC router
#   - no SSR entrypoint (no entry.server.*, no server.*)
#   - no @react-router/* server packages in frontend/package.json
#   - no createStaticHandler / renderToPipeableStream anywhere in src/
# There is no server-side action pipeline for the bypass to act on.
#
# The fix requires react-router-dom 7.x -> 8.3.0, a major upgrade across 25+
# dashboard routes. That is tracked as planned work rather than rushed in
# under an advisory that does not apply here — the migration's regression
# surface is materially larger than this exposure.
#
# REMOVE THIS ENTRY when react-router-dom reaches >= 8.3.0.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
